.TH MOUNT 2
.SH NAME
mount - install a registered native filesystem mount
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <astia/api/syscalls.h>
.PP
.B long astia_mount(const char *type, const char *target, const char *source);
.SH DESCRIPTION
Installs the registered filesystem type at target.  Target is normalized and
must name an existing directory; source is an opaque filesystem-specific name
and may be null.  This interface changes only the in-memory Astia VFS and does
not access or persist a host filesystem.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero on success or a negative Astia errno.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EFAULT
A supplied string is not readable userspace memory.
.TP
.B EINVAL
An argument is null (except source), or target is not an absolute path.
.TP
.B EEXIST
Target is already a mount point.
.TP
.B ENOENT
Target does not exist.
.TP
.B EBUSY
The fixed mount table has no available slot or the operation conflicts with a mount.
.TP
.B EPERM
The effective UID is not zero.
.TP
.B ENODEV
Type is not registered.
